From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: a shortcut's menu verb runs on its target

The item menu (the desktop's icons, File Explorer) ran a registry verb with
the file's class: for a shortcut, "lnkfile" -- its command ran the .lnk
itself, and "Run as administrator" on a shortcut started nothing (David
2026-10-02). For a shortcut the class is left out, so ShellExecute resolves
it and the verb applies to its target ("runas": elevated, 0444).

Gate: sg-shell's test/runas-check.sh (with defaults/43-sg-runas.reg; mutant
SG_MUTANT_LINK_VERB_CLASS fails it).
---
--- a/dlls/shell32/shlview_cmenu.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shlview_cmenu.c
@@ -417,6 +417,18 @@
         info.fMask = SEE_MASK_IDLIST | SEE_MASK_CLASSNAME;
         info.lpIDList = abs_pidl;
         info.lpClass = menu->filetype;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_LINK_VERB_CLASS
+        /* Stained Glass OS: a shortcut's verb (Run as administrator, from
+         * the desktop or File Explorer) is its target's: without the class,
+         * ShellExecute resolves the shortcut (and "runas" elevates the
+         * target, 0444); with "lnkfile" it ran the .lnk itself, and nothing
+         * started (David 2026-10-02) */
+        if (!wcsicmp( menu->filetype, L"lnkfile" ))
+        {
+            info.fMask = SEE_MASK_IDLIST;
+            info.lpClass = NULL;
+        }
+#endif
         info.hwnd = hwnd;
         info.nShow = SW_SHOWNORMAL;
         info.lpVerb = verb;
